Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggvis/c/YOIrPK9yCe0/m/8tBRoNvxXqMJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Aran,

There have been a lot of changes to httpuv, shiny and ggvis since
August so I'd recommend updating to the latest version from github.  I
tried your code with the latest and didn't see those problems.

Also the memory reported by the OS is a bit unreliable (as described
in http://adv-r.had.co.nz/memory.html#total-memory-use), instead try
this function:

mem <- function() {
  bit <- 8L * .Machine$sizeof.pointer
  if (bit != 32L && bit != 64L) {
    stop("Unknown architecture", call. = FALSE)
  }

  node_size <- if (bit == 32L) 28L else 56L

  usage <- gc()
  sum(usage[, 1] * c(node_size, 8)) / (1024 ^ 2)
}
mem()

Hadley

